      ":question/problem": "![](images/76/7652a5143baffd1402ffe3d240ee5e3d6b0e529dd7632d3760de85a5b2c83300.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $L$ lies on the segment $XW$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OX}=c$ and $\\overrightarrow{OW}=d$. The lengths satisfy $XL:LW=4:5$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OL}$ in terms of $c$ and $d$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OX}=c\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OW}=d .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $X$ through $O$ to $W$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{XW}=\\overrightarrow{XO}+\\overrightarrow{OW}=-c+d.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $XL:LW=4:5$ gives $9$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{XL}=\\frac{4}{9}\\overrightarrow{XW}=\\frac{4}{9}(-c+d).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to X\\to L$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OL}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XL}\\\\&=c+\\frac{4}{9}(-c+d)\\\\&=\\frac{5}{9}c+\\frac{4}{9}d.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
